<title>USA: Biomatrix signs Synvisc marketing pact.</title>
<headline>Biomatrix signs Synvisc marketing pact.</headline>
<dateline>RIDGEFIELD, N.J. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biomatrix Inc said it signed an agreement with Boehringer Ingelheim to market and distribute Synvisc in France, Algeria, Morocco and Tunisia for up to 15 years.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Boehringer Ingelheim will pay a licensing fee of up to $8 million to Biomatrix. The fee includes up-front fees and milestone payments at certain sales volumes, Biomatrix said. The sales volumes weren't disclosed.</p>
<p>Boehringer plans to launch Synvisc in France in early 1997, Biomatrix said. Synvisc is used to treat osteoarthritis of the knee and is based on Biomatrix' hylan technology.</p>
</text>
